cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FreeNIC: Free National Information Center"
message: "If you use this data, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Anderson
    given-names: Nicholas
    email: nickawebbox@gmail.com
    affiliation: "The New School for Social Research"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # Nick to fill
repository-code: "https://github.com/andenick/FreeNIC"
url: "https://freenic.org"
abstract: >-
  FreeNIC is a research-grade, openly published U.S. banking data warehouse that
  harmonizes the major public regulatory sources - FFIEC Call Reports & UBPR,
  FDIC (BankFind, SDI, Summary of Deposits, historical), the Federal Reserve
  (FR Y-9C/BHCF, H.8, FRED), OCC, NCUA, SEC EDGAR, and derived academic panels -
  into a single provenance-tracked warehouse with a harmonized variable
  dictionary. The public data release (v1.0.0) ships 61 files (60 base Parquet
  tables plus the 1863-2026 bank-aggregate spine); totals are approximately
  4.97 billion rows across 21 source families, spanning 1782-2026, covering
  217,210 institutions and 87,351 MDRM variables. Code is MIT; the data
  compilation is CC-BY-4.0.
keywords:
  - banking
  - regulatory-data
  - ffiec
  - fdic
  - federal-reserve
  - open-data
version: "1.0.0"
